// case: config-port-string
// what: a `port` config declaration whose value is a string, not an integer.
//
// The declaration used to be parsed and then discarded entirely, so any value
// at all was accepted and the server always bound 3000. The value is now the
// default port the built server binds, which means it has to be a port: an
// integer literal in 1..65535. "8080" is not one, and saying so at compile
// time is cheaper than a service that comes up on the wrong port.
port "8080"
// expect-error: takes an integer literal
